Use the native i386 x87 for the calibrated Wine FIR arithmetic. The software
64-significand-bit implementation is retained for WASM and non-i386 builds.
Twenty 16 kHz voices at 44.1 kHz took longer to mix than their real duration;
ASan's extra overhead caused elapsed-time catch-up to starve loaded races.
The native FIR temporarily selects nearest/even, 64-bit x87 precision, performs
each operation at that precision and retains the original explicit Float32
spills. Restore the caller's control word before returning to engine physics.
No PCM, source cursor, gain, service or elapsed-time block is dropped.

